{"title":"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 40","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Magic_Formula)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Magic Formula)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4(Answer_Choices,_Approximation)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4(Answer Choices, Approximation)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_40&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Located inside equilateral triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/7/4875554552d7960e8b12539fdb3b6a8e8adee48a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PA=8$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/6/2261d7187fda863485664fcec25000f556f954f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PB=6$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/d/e1d04195fd09d1f6a5472344027a7b658716c2e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PC=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />.  To the nearest integer the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/5/0b5c444160e43bf4cdda46a2619ebac72c270c79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 159\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 131\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 95\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 79\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"412\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_40&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/f/d2fa9974822bde06c4ef64cbfa757859bb2c2d19.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((0,10)--(8.66,-5)--(-8.66,-5)--cycle); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(0,10),N); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,(-9.5,-5.2),N); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,(9.5,-5.2),N);  dot((-3,0)); label(&quot;$P$&quot;,(-3,-2),N); draw((-3,0)--(0,10)); draw((-3,0)--(-8.66,-5)); draw((-3,0)--(8.66,-5));  dot((-9,7.5)); label(&quot;$P&#39;$&quot;,(-9.2,7.5),N); draw((-9,7.5)--(0,10)); draw((-9,7.5)--(-8.66,-5)); draw((-9,7.5)--(-3,0));  [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"205\" />\n</p><p>Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/9/af95ce663bb1312dc2fc6fc91d2c39c361fbd5f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^2+8^2=10^2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"18\" /> That makes us want to construct a right triangle.\n</p><p>Rotate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/5/14589098013cf51bd13b7d32a5476db3ee28f0cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle APC$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/d/08d5c45388de5c75af641c046d466de3592ffa98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> about A. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/d/b8d53a0e945b7717a0ce3108b3d06532e333f3ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PAC \\cong \\triangle P&#39;AB$\" width=\"145\" height=\"14\" />, so \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/a/86a1830894571b000781fa58851431e940d8cc7b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle P&#39;AP = \\angle PAB + \\angle P&#39;AB = \\angle PAB + \\angle PAC = 60^{\\circ}.\\]\" width=\"431\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/4/0a46cce1a84b33ea3685e82599c8b946943ba546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle APP&#39;$\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" /> is equilateral, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/5/8e506bf8d32059d87ab50776563c82f16e6218fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P&#39;P=8$\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" />, which means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e12f779b757cc822e8b647183b398b887a27524.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle P&#39;PB = 90^{\\circ}.$\" width=\"114\" height=\"14\" /> \n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/7/c17e404d46e8a76c800da6d918b949f014efbb61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BP&#39;P = \\alpha .$\" width=\"100\" height=\"14\" /> Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/2/5b2c894cf6bd11b6faeed9acaf909f3b06aa0bc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos\\alpha = \\frac{8}{10}=\\frac{4}{5},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"127\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/8/46842c6049501ec759f044c7f7884fd810ae4b5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin\\alpha = \\frac{3}{5}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"78\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Applying the Law of Cosines to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/5/14589098013cf51bd13b7d32a5476db3ee28f0cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle APC$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> (remembering <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/9/7a9db35d9d1e5aefd7c4d47e1b00bfed7a63a299.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle APC = \\angle AP&#39;B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"141\" height=\"16\" />):\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/a/81a12c0669c33e6f8fcc0177d86e1a1394706739.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} AC^2 &amp;= 10^2+8^2-2\\cdot10\\cdot8\\cdot \\cos(60^{\\circ}+\\alpha)\\\\&amp;= 164-160(\\cos60\\cos\\alpha-\\sin60\\sin\\alpha)\\\\&amp;= 164-160(\\frac{2}{5}-\\frac{3\\sqrt3}{10}) \\\\&amp;= 164-16(4-3\\sqrt3) \\\\ &amp;= 100+48\\sqrt3.\\end{align*}\" width=\"342\" height=\"149\" />\n</p><p>We want to find the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/e/4be47242dd8ef0f2732441efceafde99e8dee215.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AC^2\\cdot\\frac{\\sqrt3}{4}=25\\sqrt3+36\\approx\\boxed{(D) 79}.\\]\" width=\"270\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>~pfalcon\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Magic_Formula.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Magic_Formula)\">Solution 2 (Magic Formula)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_40&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Magic Formula)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Fun formula:  Given a point whose distances from the vertices of an equilateral triangle are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, the side length of the triangle is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/9/db99a355e83e210009718fc38eb1f26afe7ba4dd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[s=\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}\\left(a^2+b^2+c^2\\pm\\sqrt{6(a^2b^2+b^2c^2+c^2a^2)-3(a^4+b^4+c^4)}\\right)}\\]\" width=\"525\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>Given that the area of an equilateral triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/f/92fe9758cda7434b713a2a906f0931971f4aff4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}s^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"42\" height=\"41\" />, the answer is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/a/fea79c2ee9cea5f154a4537c0d9adc5d110e0ccf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} [ABC] &amp;= \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}\\left(a^2+b^2+c^2\\pm\\sqrt{6(a^2b^2+b^2c^2+c^2a^2)-3(a^4+b^4+c^4)}\\right)\\\\ &amp;= \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{8}\\left(200\\pm\\sqrt{6\\cdot 16(3^2 4^2+4^2 5^2+5^2 3^2)-3\\cdot16(3^4+4^4+5^4)}\\right)\\\\ &amp;= \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{8}\\left(200\\pm\\sqrt{96(144+400+225)-48(81+256+625)}\\right)\\\\ &amp;= \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{8}\\left(200\\pm\\sqrt{96\\cdot769-48\\cdot962}\\right) = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{8}\\left(200\\pm\\sqrt{96\\cdot769-96\\cdot481}\\right)\\\\ &amp;= \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{8}\\left(200\\pm\\sqrt{96\\cdot288}\\right) = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{8}\\left(200\\pm\\sqrt{96\\cdot96\\cdot3}\\right)\\\\ &amp;= 25\\sqrt{3}\\pm36 \\approx \\{6.5, \\text{or } 78.5\\} \\end{align*}\" width=\"609\" height=\"274\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/1/7314f8133d3b925b9ce6598191d153da7ecdd779.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6.5$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" /> is not a choice, therefore the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/c/ddca304a80bcdc7a8527ff9470e67402dcdb802f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }79}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"67\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>(Note that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/1/7314f8133d3b925b9ce6598191d153da7ecdd779.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6.5$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" /> answer is actually the solution for when point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is <i>exterior</i> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />.)\n</p><p>~proloto\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_40&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Rotate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/d/08d5c45388de5c75af641c046d466de3592ffa98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> CCW around <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, becoming <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.  Rotate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/d/08d5c45388de5c75af641c046d466de3592ffa98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> CCW around <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, becoming <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />.  Rotate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/d/08d5c45388de5c75af641c046d466de3592ffa98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> CCW around <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, becoming <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/1/ed1800bd218c64918b46da7d925a5c5ad95a0443.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import graph; import geometry; size(12cm);  pair A, B, C, P, X, Y, Z;  // Define the equilateral triangle ABC real a = sqrt(100+48*sqrt(3)); A = (0, 0); B = rotate(60)*A + (a, 0); C = rotate(120)*B + (a, 0);  // Define point P using given distances pair[] P_candidates = intersectionpoints(Circle(A,8), Circle(B,6)); for (pair candidate : P_candidates) {     if (length(candidate - C) &lt; 10.1 &amp;&amp; length(candidate - C) &gt; 9.9) {         P = candidate;         break;     } }  // Rotate C and P about A through 60 degrees to get B and X X = rotate(60,A)*P;  // Rotate A and P about B through 60 degrees to get C and Y Y = rotate(60,B)*P;  // Rotate B and P about C through 60 degrees to get A and Z Z = rotate(60,C)*P;  // Draw the triangle and the segments draw(A--B--C--cycle); draw(A--P); draw(B--P); draw(C--P);  // Connect X, Y, Z to P and to the vertices of the triangle draw(X--P, dashed); draw(Y--P, dashed); draw(Z--P, dashed); draw(X--A, dashed); draw(X--C, dashed); draw(Y--A, dashed); draw(Y--B, dashed); draw(Z--B, dashed); draw(Z--C, dashed);  // Label the points label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, SW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, SE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, N); label(&quot;$P$&quot;, P, NNE*2); label(&quot;$X$&quot;, X, NW); label(&quot;$Y$&quot;, Y, S); label(&quot;$Z$&quot;, Z, E);  // Add the distances label(&quot;$8$&quot;, (A+P)/2, NW); label(&quot;$6$&quot;, (B+P)/2, NE); label(&quot;$10$&quot;, (C+P)/2, N);  // Add right angle marks draw(rightanglemark(C,X,P,15)); draw(rightanglemark(P,B,Z,15)); draw(rightanglemark(A,P,Y,15)); [/asy]\" width=\"568\" height=\"565\" />\n</p><p>Notice that since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/a/f2a3d5ea0a26c76f79be320d9e823aca5ae6c5b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AXC\\cong\\triangle APB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"145\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/6/576c41208ebaca6cb0a5899fd86848d58cc75697.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BYA\\cong\\triangle BPC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"145\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/3/ed3ed1044f6dd1dab72afe37e8ee2d76ddfc428f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CZB\\cong\\triangle CPA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"143\" height=\"18\" />, then\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/6/22697db0983b58ae901e62a0e2ed826400d6488b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[AYBZCX]=2\\cdot[ABC]\\]\" width=\"193\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Now the area of the big hexagon is easy to compute since it's comprised of 3 equilateral triangle and 3 right triangles:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/7/267437f300e2d596b8ce20112de023ddc0eb6f2c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}[ABC] &amp;= \\frac{1}{2}[AYBZCX] = \\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\underbrace{3\\cdot\\frac12\\cdot6\\cdot8}_{\\text{3 right triangles}}+\\underbrace{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\left(6^2+8^2+10^2\\right)}_{\\text{3 equilateral triangles}}\\right)\\\\ &amp;= \\frac{1}{2}\\left(72+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\cdot200)\\right) = 36+25\\sqrt{3}\\\\ &amp;\\approx \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }79} \\end{align*}\" width=\"516\" height=\"181\" />\n</p><p>~proloto\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4.28Answer_Choices.2C_Approximation.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4(Answer_Choices,_Approximation)\">Solution 4(Answer Choices, Approximation)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_40&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4(Answer Choices, Approximation)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the side length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/2/bd222166def59a3315433877917a826de6488031.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/d/00d8839e7bd7b8f0edfa7d32e0ddc285c7b310a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s\\le 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"53\" height=\"16\" /> by the triangle inequality. This means that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/d/0dda7d5d4b5e92bb95907a255e63349df41d27dd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[ABC]\\le\\dfrac{14^2\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\approx 84.87.\\]\" width=\"197\" height=\"41\" /> This automatically rules out choices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/f/ccf6d387ce491c0ca100c134021f21f616d75162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/2/792daa030c96693198f143f9176bf888b7ca25cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C.$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> Now, we will look at if the area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. By the equilateral triangle area formula, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> would equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/7/4b7b1b7c42d6c24a8da912d5b6394a2dc6700bbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10\\sqrt{\\dfrac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}}\\approx 10.75.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"137\" height=\"56\" /> This is very close to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/3/b833a70e5b34465a7e1cc445231d569f21b81da4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/061c787348178cb1c620b54758f8e7f965201268.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s=10,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"17\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/5/45510291c2a3a50e21b1cfbe7edfb5cbbb47a161.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle APB=90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"100\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/1/a71cc8f1a6f837dd01437015e45340bfdab4a3c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle APC, \\angle BPC&lt;90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"162\" height=\"18\" /> by the Pythagorean theorem and Pythagorean inequalities. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/f/3af772a77ee4d7e9fa8c0a60f2c7722c57d85324.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle APB+\\angle APC+\\angle BPC&lt;270.\\]\" width=\"265\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/3/8f3e5fe3d3a6efec7643b703dfa63f4ec7c5a541.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle APB+\\angle APC+\\angle BPC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"213\" height=\"16\" /> needs to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/1/a1119a7d1df3b1832c1c88407eb7c8e13893f6ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$360,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"17\" /> and it probably cannot increase by more than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcfee7bd8a5e15e5f6b7881c138de43651572a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> by just adding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/4/274c3ed420a60124420c39b147c9a39b6778d0f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.75$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> (more rigorous proof below) Thus, the only viable answer choice is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/5/a351c0db84d00018a3dd486a7a905f97e00f6b59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{79}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"36\" height=\"25\" />\n</p>\n<ul><li>In fact, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/d/d4d840dd495eb33382c066af64a02cb9f8c07374.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s&lt;\\sqrt{136}\\approx 11.66$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"143\" height=\"21\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/0/740a542ce6cddbcf215abce2c661bb10c767ae7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABC]&lt;34\\sqrt{3}\\approx58.88$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"187\" height=\"24\" />) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/1/a71cc8f1a6f837dd01437015e45340bfdab4a3c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle APC, \\angle BPC&lt;90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"162\" height=\"18\" /> still holds. As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/6/886e0e52392c0f69215e570e0f6afd61a74272cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle APB &lt;180,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/6/d460022b3d28c482cb3e0c2b54da20e3895250bd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle APB+\\angle APC+\\angle BPC&lt;360.\\]\" width=\"265\" height=\"14\" /> Thus, we know for sure that the nearest integer to the area cannot be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/3/f6396a14d58628924f3cc5e52c29ae4aa8b0e7b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50.$\" width=\"21\" height=\"12\" /></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_40&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME\" title=\"1967 AHSME\">1967 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1967 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1967\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_39\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 39\">Pro